  "notes": "Composed of {降|こう} (descend) and {下|か} (down). Describes a downward movement or decrease, used in both physical and measurable contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {気温|きおん}の{降下|こうか}: temperature drop\n- {血圧|けつあつ}の{降下|こうか}: blood pressure drop\n- {降下|こうか}{訓練|くんれん}: descent training (parachute)\n- {急降下|きゅうこうか}: nosedive, steep descent\n- {落下傘|らっかさん}{降下|こうか}: parachute descent\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {低下|ていか}: decline, deterioration — used for quality, ability, or levels declining over time\n- {降下|こうか}: descent, drop — emphasizes physical downward movement or sudden decrease\n- {下降|かこう}: descent, going down — more neutral term for downward movement\n- {落下|らっか}: falling — an object dropping due to gravity\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal and technical. Common in news reports, medical contexts, and military terminology. In everyday speech, {下|さ}がる is more natural for describing drops in temperature or pressure.",
